{
  "$schema": "./method-table.schema.json",
  "ariVersion": "1.0.0",
  "methods": [
    {
      "name": "initialize",
      "direction": "host_to_driver",
      "kind": "request",
      "params": {
        "$ref": "handshake.schema.json#/$defs/InitializeParams"
      },
      "result": {
        "$ref": "handshake.schema.json#/$defs/InitializeResult"
      },
      "version": {
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0
      },
      "notes": "First message on a connection. Negotiates the contract version, the event grammar version (highest version in both ranges), per-method versions and the persistence version. A method whose major version differs between the two sides is refused on its own, and so is a method whose helper (a stream's item notification, a delegated child's process methods) is refused or not listed by the driver. The core methods initialize, stream/end and stream/cancel are the exception: no stream can end or be stopped without them, so a driver that does not list one (detail core_method_missing) or a major mismatch on one (core_method_version_mismatch) refuses the connection. Other refusals: ari_version_mismatch, grammar_version_mismatch, persistence_version_mismatch. After a refusal the driver is still uninitialized and the host may send initialize again."
    },
    {
      "name": "stream/end",
      "direction": "both",
      "kind": "notification",
      "params": {
        "$ref": "rpc.schema.json#/$defs/StreamEndParams"
      },
      "version": {
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0
      },
      "notes": "The producer of a stream ends it, with an error when it failed. A producer sends a stream's notifications only after the response that carries its streamId."
    },
    {
      "name": "stream/cancel",
      "direction": "both",
      "kind": "request",
      "params": {
        "$ref": "rpc.schema.json#/$defs/StreamCancelParams"
      },
      "result": {
        "$ref": "rpc.schema.json#/$defs/VoidResult"
      },
      "version": {
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0
      },
      "notes": "The consumer of a stream stops it early. The producer answers null and then sends stream/end. Cancelling a stream that already ended, or that the producer does not know, also answers null."
    },
    {
